-- name    : FoundationsRL.TabularRL.ucbvi_regret_bound
-- status  : Open
-- author  : @iris
-- created : 2026-10-30T21:22:07.210228+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/fdbb17c9-56e4-497d-a143-d9ab3ae9490e
-- title:
--   Theorem 1 — UCB-VI has regret $\lesssim HS\sqrt{AT}\sqrt{\log(SAHT/\delta)}$ with probability $\ge1-\delta$ (corrected: $V^{M,\star}_h\in[0,1]$ at every layer; $\bar Q_{H+1}\equiv0$)
-- statement:
--   There is an absolute constant $C>0$ with the following property. Let $M$ be a finite-horizon episodic MDP with $S$ states, $A\ge1$ actions and horizon $H$, whose rewards are deterministic, known and in $[0,1]$, and whose optimal values satisfy $V^{M,\star}_h(s)\in[0,1]$ for every layer $h\in[H]$ and state $s$ (Assumption 6, corrected). Let $T\in\mathbb N$ and $\delta>0$, and run UCB-VI for $T$ episodes with the bonus
--
--   $$
--   b^t_{h,\delta}(s,a)=2\sqrt{\frac{\log(2SAHT/\delta)}{n^t_h(s,a)}}
--   $$
--
--   and any tie-breaking rule. Then with probability at least $1-\delta$,
--
--   $$
--   \mathrm{Reg}=\sum_{t=1}^T f^M(\pi_M)-f^M(\widehat\pi^t)\le C\cdot HS\sqrt{AT}\cdot\sqrt{\log(SAHT/\delta)}.
--   $$
--
--   This is the first regret bound for reinforcement learning in the notes: optimism, implemented by bonuses added to value iteration on an estimated model, gives regret polynomial in the numbers of states and actions and in the horizon, where uniform exploration can need a number of episodes exponential in $H$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $\mathrm{Reg}$ is the pseudo-regret of the played policies; the probability is over the $T$-episode history generated by UCB-VI in $M$, computed as a finite sum over histories.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--
--   - correction: Assumption 6 (p. 89) bounds only the initial value, $V^{M,\star}_1(s)\in[0,1]$ → $V^{M,\star}_h(s)\in[0,1]$ for every layer $h\in[H]$ and state $s$; reason: the printed theorem is false: $H=3$, states $s_0,u,g,b,z$, two actions, $d_1=\delta_{s_0}$; at layer 1, $s_0$ moves to $u$ or $z$ with probability $1/2$ each and every other state to $z$, rewards 0; at layer 2, $u$ gives reward 1 and the good action moves to $g$, the other to $b$, other states give 0 and move to $z$; at layer 3, reward 1 at $g$, 0 elsewhere. Then $V^{M,\star}_1\le1$ but $V^{M,\star}_2(u)=2$, both actions at $u$ have $\bar Q^t_2=1$ in every episode, and a tie-break that never picks the good action has regret $T/2$, which no bound of order $\sqrt T$ covers
--   - correction: the algorithm box (p. 89) sets $\bar V^t_{H+1}\equiv1$ → $\bar Q^t_{H+1}\equiv0$, as in (5.29) and the proof of Lemma 16; reason: with $\bar V^t_{H+1}\equiv1$ and $r\ge0$, every $\bar Q^t_h\equiv1$, so the played policy is the fixed tie-break; for $S=H=1$, two actions with rewards 0 and 1 and a tie-break choosing the first, the regret is $T$
--   - generalization: $H\ge1$, $T\ge1$ implicitly → any $H,T\in\mathbb N$; reason: at $H=0$ or $T=0$ the regret and the bound are both 0; the source's statement is the special case $H,T\ge1$
--   - encoding: $\mathrm{Reg}\lesssim HS\sqrt{AT}\sqrt{\log(SAHT/\delta)}$ → $\exists C>0$ quantified before the types, the MDP and all parameters, with $\mathrm{Reg}\le C\,HS\sqrt{AT}\sqrt{\log(SAHT/\delta)}$; reason: $\lesssim$ hides an absolute constant
--   - encoding: bonus $+\infty$ at $n^t_h(s,a)=0$ → clipped value $\bar Q^t_h(s,a)=1$ at unvisited pairs (published `ucbQ`); reason: $\{\cdot+\infty\}\wedge1=1$; same algorithm
--   - encoding: $\widehat\pi^t_h(s)=\arg\max_a\bar Q^t_h(s,a)$ → any maximizer, chosen by an arbitrary, possibly history-dependent selector; reason: the source does not fix a tie-breaking rule; every rule is covered
--   - encoding: deterministic known rewards $r_h$, with probability over the episodes → the MDP's mean rewards `M.R` given to the algorithm; probability as a finite sum over $T$-episode histories (`probEvent`); $0$-indexed layers and episodes; reason: Lean conventions of the published `FoundationsRL_RLBasics_Core` and `UCBVI_v2`; same instances
-- source:
--   Foster & Rakhlin, Foundations of Reinforcement Learning and Interactive Decision Making, arXiv:2312.16730v1, Theorem 1, Eq. (5.27), p. 90; algorithm box UCB-VI and Assumption 6, p. 89

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_FoundationsRL_RLBasics_Core
import Definitions.Def_FoundationsRL_RLBasics_UCBVI_v2
import Definitions.Def_FoundationsRL_TabularRL_IsUCBVI
import Definitions.Def_FoundationsRL_TabularRL_regret

universe u

namespace FoundationsRL.TabularRL

open FoundationsRL.RLBasics

/-- **Theorem 1** (Foster & Rakhlin, *Foundations of Reinforcement Learning and Interactive
Decision Making*, arXiv:2312.16730v1, Theorem 1, p. 90): there is an absolute constant `C` such
that for every finite tabular MDP satisfying Assumption 6 (corrected), every `T`, and every
`δ > 0`, UCB-VI with the bonus (5.27) `b^t_{h,δ}(s,a) = 2√(log(2SAHT/δ)/n^t_h(s,a))` has, with
probability at least `1 − δ`,
`Reg ≤ C · H S √(AT) · √(log(SAHT/δ))`.

Assumption 6 (p. 89, corrected): rewards are deterministic, known and in `[0,1]`, and
`V^{M,⋆}_h(s) ∈ [0,1]` for every layer `h ∈ [H]` and state `s`.

**Formalization Note.** The book's `≲` hides an absolute constant: `∃ C` is quantified before
every type, MDP and parameter. `S, A` in the bound are `Fintype.card S`, `Fintype.card A`; the
initial distribution `d1` forces `S` nonempty and `[Nonempty A]` is the book's standing
non-empty action set. Rewards are deterministic and known, so the MDP's mean reward `M.R` is the
reward function and is the one the algorithm uses. `Reg` is the pseudo-regret of the played
policies (`regret`), and the probability is over the `T`-episode history generated by the
learner in `M` (`probEvent`). `IsUCBVI` allows any tie-breaking rule in the `arg max`.
Correction: Assumption 6 as printed bounds only `V^{M,⋆}_1`; the theorem is false under that
assumption (counterexample in the item's differences). -/
theorem ucbvi_regret_bound :
    ∃ C : ℝ, 0 < C ∧
      ∀ {S A : Type u} [Fintype S] [Fintype A] [Nonempty A] [DecidableEq S] [DecidableEq A]
        {H : ℕ} (M : EpisodicMDP S A H) (T : ℕ) (δ : ℝ) (learner : Learner S A H),
        0 < δ →
        (∀ h, h < H → ∀ s a, 0 ≤ M.R h s a ∧ M.R h s a ≤ 1) →
        (∀ h, h < H → ∀ s, 0 ≤ Vstar M h s ∧ Vstar M h s ≤ 1) →
        IsUCBVI M M.R δ T learner →
        1 - δ ≤ probEvent M learner T (fun histT =>
          regret M learner T histT ≤
            C * H * Fintype.card S * Real.sqrt (Fintype.card A * T) *
              Real.sqrt (Real.log (Fintype.card S * Fintype.card A * H * T / δ))) := by sorry

end FoundationsRL.TabularRL
